---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Nimbus vs Other Media Offload Plugins — Side-by-Side Comparison"
  description="See how Nimbus compares to other WordPress media offload plugins. Free and open source, with pauseable bulk jobs, built-in cache purge, cost analytics, and no per-file caps."
>
  <Navbar />

  <main id="main-content" class="compare-page">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="compare-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="section-label">Comparison</p>
        <h1 class="compare-headline">Why developers are switching to Nimbus</h1>
        <p class="compare-sub">
          The market leader still starts at $99/yr and doesn't support
          Cloudflare R2. A newer wave of free plugins has shown up too — but
          most of them save their best features (bulk migration, cache purge,
          WooCommerce downloads) for a paid upgrade. Nimbus doesn't: every
          feature is free, unlimited, on every install.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Key differentiator banner -->
    <section class="diff-banner">
      <div class="container diff-banner-inner">
        <div class="diff-item diff-item--us">
          <span class="diff-label">Nimbus</span>
          <p class="diff-heading">Free, unlimited, every feature included</p>
          <p class="diff-body">
            Upload 1 file or 1 million, run 1 site or 100 — there is no price,
            no license key, and no feature held back behind a paid tier.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="diff-vs">vs</div>
        <div class="diff-item diff-item--them">
          <span class="diff-label">Other plugins</span>
          <p class="diff-heading">Free to install, paid to actually use</p>
          <p class="diff-body">
            The traditional players charge per media item, with hard caps
            that force an upgrade as your library grows. The newer free
            plugins usually keep bulk migration, cache purging, or
            WooCommerce integration behind their own paid tier.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Free vs. free -->
    <section class="section section--alt">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="section-headline" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem">
          Not every free plugin is actually free to use
        </h2>
        <p class="section-sub" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">
          A few other WordPress media offload plugins now offer a free tier
          too. The difference is what's actually included in it.
        </p>

        <div class="compare-table-wrap">
          <table class="compare-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="col-feature">In the free tier</th>
                <th class="col-nimbus">
                  <span class="th-brand th-brand--nimbus">Nimbus</span>
                </th>
                <th class="col-them">
                  <span class="th-brand th-brand--them">Typical free-tier plugin</span>
                </th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Bulk migration of existing library</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Unlimited, pause/resume, live progress</td>
                <td class="col-them">Often a paid add-on, or capped batch size</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Cache purge automation</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Cloudflare, LiteSpeed, WP Fastest Cache, proxy</td>
                <td class="col-them">Rarely included at all</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>WooCommerce signed downloads</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Included</td>
                <td class="col-them">Commonly a paid add-on</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Page-builder / gallery DB rewriting</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Elementor, Slider Revolution, Smart Slider 3, NextGEN</td>
                <td class="col-them">Rarely included at all</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Storage cost analytics</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Included</td>
                <td class="col-them">Rarely included at all</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Multisite network admin panel</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Included</td>
                <td class="col-them">Rarely included at all</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>REST API + WP-CLI</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Full read/write endpoints, full CLI suite</td>
                <td class="col-them">CLI sometimes present; REST API rarely</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="compare-footnote">
          Based on published feature lists and pricing pages of currently
          active WordPress.org media offload plugins as of mid-2026. Always
          check a plugin's current listing before switching — free tiers
          change over time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Pricing table -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="section-headline" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem">
          And against the traditional paid plugins
        </h2>
        <p class="section-sub" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">
          Competitor prices are representative of the leading per-file pricing
          plugins at regular (non-promo) rates, shown annually.
        </p>

        <div class="compare-table-wrap">
          <table class="compare-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="col-feature">Plan</th>
                <th class="col-nimbus">
                  <span class="th-brand th-brand--nimbus">Nimbus</span>
                </th>
                <th class="col-them">
                  <span class="th-brand th-brand--them">Other plugins</span>
                </th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Price</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <strong>$0 / forever</strong>
                  <span class="td-note"
                    >Unlimited sites · unlimited media · every feature</span
                  >
                </td>
                <td class="col-them">
                  <span class="dash">—</span>
                  <span class="td-note">$99–$1,199/yr depending on media volume</span>
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Media file cap</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <strong>None</strong>
                  <span class="td-note">Unlimited on every install</span>
                </td>
                <td class="col-them">
                  <strong>Hard cap per plan</strong>
                  <span class="td-note"
                    >2K → 500K, paid extra for unlimited</span
                  >
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Feature matrix -->
    <section class="section section--alt">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="section-headline" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">
          Feature comparison
        </h2>

        <div class="compare-table-wrap">
          <table class="compare-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="col-feature">Feature</th>
                <th class="col-nimbus">
                  <span class="th-brand th-brand--nimbus">Nimbus</span>
                </th>
                <th class="col-them">
                  <span class="th-brand th-brand--them">Other plugins</span>
                </th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <!-- Pricing & Limits -->
              <tr class="compare-category-row"><td colspan="3">Pricing &amp; Limits</td></tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Media file cap</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">None — unlimited on all plans</td>
                <td class="col-them">Hard cap per plan (2K → 500K → paid extra for unlimited)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Free plan</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> 1 site · unlimited media · no time limit</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span> Paid only</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>License model</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">Free — no license, no media cap</td>
                <td class="col-them">Per media item count · unlimited sites</td>
              </tr>

              <!-- Storage Providers -->
              <tr class="compare-category-row"><td colspan="3">Storage Providers</td></tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Amazon S3</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus"><span class="check">✓</span> Included</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="check">✓</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Cloudflare R2</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Dedicated profile — endpoint, region &amp; path-style pre-configured from your Account ID</td>
                <td class="col-them">Manual S3-compatible setup</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Google Cloud Storage</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Dedicated profile via HMAC XML API</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="check">✓</span> Varies by plugin</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>DigitalOcean Spaces</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus"><span class="check">✓</span> Dedicated profile</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="check">✓</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Backblaze B2</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Dedicated profile</td>
                <td class="col-them">Varies by plugin</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Wasabi</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Dedicated profile</td>
                <td class="col-them">Varies by plugin</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>MinIO (self-hosted)</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Dedicated profile</td>
                <td class="col-them">Generic S3-compat only</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Any S3-compatible provider</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Generic profile</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="check">✓</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Create bucket from WordPress</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> No cloud console needed</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span> Must create manually</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Switch providers without URL changes</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Change a setting — done</td>
                <td class="col-them">Full database search-replace required</td>
              </tr>

              <!-- Media Delivery -->
              <tr class="compare-category-row"><td colspan="3">Media Delivery</td></tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Automatic URL rewriting</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Included</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="check">✓</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Custom CDN delivery domain</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Point to any CDN edge or subdomain</td>
                <td class="col-them">Varies by plugin</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Toggle cloud / local serving instantly</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> One click — no post edits</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>

              <!-- Migration & Scheduling -->
              <tr class="compare-category-row"><td colspan="3">Migration &amp; Scheduling</td></tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Bulk migrate existing library</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Included</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="check">✓</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Pause &amp; resume bulk migration</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Survives server restarts</td>
                <td class="col-them">Simple background only, no pause/resume</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Live migration progress stream</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Real-time SSE updates</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Nightly off-hours scheduling</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Configurable time · up to 8 workers</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Restore files back to local server</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Included</td>
                <td class="col-them">Varies by plugin</td>
              </tr>

              <!-- Offload Rules -->
              <tr class="compare-category-row"><td colspan="3">Offload Rules</td></tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Filter by MIME type</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Included</td>
                <td class="col-them">Varies by plugin</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Filter by minimum file size</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span></td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Path glob allow / deny rules</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Block or allow specific folders</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>

              <!-- Caching -->
              <tr class="compare-category-row"><td colspan="3">Cache Purging</td></tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Cloudflare cache purge</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Automatic after every offload</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>LiteSpeed &amp; WP Fastest Cache purge</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Built-in</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Nginx PURGE support</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Configurable endpoint</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>

              <!-- Analytics -->
              <tr class="compare-category-row"><td colspan="3">Analytics</td></tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Storage usage dashboard</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> MIME breakdown · trend charts</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>S3 vs R2 cost comparison</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Live estimate from your library size</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>

              <!-- Integrations -->
              <tr class="compare-category-row"><td colspan="3">Integrations</td></tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Page-builder URL rewriting (Elementor, etc.)</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Included</td>
                <td class="col-them">Separate paid add-ons</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>WooCommerce signed download URLs</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Included</td>
                <td class="col-them">Paid add-on required</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>WordPress Multisite (per-site settings)</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus"><span class="check">✓</span> Included</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="check">✓</span> All paid plans</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Multisite network admin panel</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Included — bird's-eye view of all sites</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>

              <!-- Developer Tools -->
              <tr class="compare-category-row"><td colspan="3">Developer &amp; Automation</td></tr>
              <tr>
                <td>WP-CLI commands</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Full wp nimbus command suite</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="check">✓</span> Basic commands</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>REST API (read + job control)</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Full endpoints — trigger jobs, query status</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>AI agent &amp; CI pipeline compatible</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Works with Claude, Cursor, GitHub Actions, n8n</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Config export / import (JSON)</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Staging → production in one step</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Live diagnostics &amp; log viewer</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner"><span class="check">✓</span> Filterable structured logs · connection test</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span></td>
              </tr>

              <!-- Support -->
              <tr class="compare-category-row"><td colspan="3">Support</td></tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Community support</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus"><span class="check">✓</span> WordPress.org forum, GitHub issues, email</td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="check">✓</span> Paid plans only</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Competitor comparison section -->
    <section class="section section--alt">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="section-headline" style="margin-bottom:0.75rem">
          How Nimbus compares to the market leader
        </h2>
        <p class="section-sub" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">
          The most popular WordPress media offload plugin on the market. Here's where Nimbus wins
          outright.
        </p>

        <div class="compare-table-wrap">
          <table class="compare-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="col-feature">Capability</th>
                <th class="col-nimbus">
                  <span class="th-brand th-brand--nimbus">Nimbus</span>
                </th>
                <th class="col-them">
                  <span class="th-brand th-brand--them">Market leader</span>
                </th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Cloudflare R2 — dedicated profile</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> Dedicated R2 profile — enter Account ID, bucket
                  &amp; API token; endpoint, region, path-style fill themselves
                </td>
                <td class="col-them"
                  >Manual S3-compatible setup, no R2-specific guidance</td
                >
              </tr>

              <tr>
                <td>Switching providers</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">Change a setting — done</td>
                <td class="col-them">Full database search-replace required</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Google Cloud Storage</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> Dedicated GCS profile via HMAC XML API
                </td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="check">✓</span> Native support</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Automatic cache purging</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> Cloudflare, LiteSpeed, WP Fastest Cache,
                  Nginx — built-in
                </td>
                <td class="col-them"
                  ><span class="dash">—</span> Not available</td
                >
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Pauseable bulk migration</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> Pause, resume, auto-retry, live SSE
                  progress stream
                </td>
                <td class="col-them"
                  >Simple background process, no pause/resume</td
                >
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Nightly off-hours scheduling</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> Configurable time · up to 8 parallel
                  workers
                </td>
                <td class="col-them"
                  ><span class="dash">—</span> Not available</td
                >
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Storage cost analytics</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> Live S3 vs R2 cost comparison by your
                  actual library size
                </td>
                <td class="col-them"
                  ><span class="dash">—</span> No cost analytics</td
                >
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Page-builder integration rewriting</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> Elementor, Slider Revolution, Smart
                  Slider 3, NextGEN — included
                </td>
                <td class="col-them">Separate paid add-ons required</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>WooCommerce signed downloads</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> Buyers redirected to signed storage URL
                  — bypasses server
                </td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="check">✓</span> Paid add-on required</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Multisite network admin</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> Per-site settings + network overview panel
                </td>
                <td class="col-them">Per-site only, no network admin panel</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Create bucket from settings page</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> Create bucket without leaving WordPress
                </td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span> Must create bucket manually</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>REST API</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> Full read + job control + presign endpoints
                </td>
                <td class="col-them">No formal REST API</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Config export / import</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> JSON backup and restore — great for staging
                </td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span> Not available</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Price</td>
                <td class="col-nimbus winner">
                  <span class="check">✓</span> Free forever, unlimited media, unlimited sites
                </td>
                <td class="col-them"><span class="dash">—</span> Paid, tiered by media volume</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container compare-faq">
        <h2 class="section-headline" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">
          Frequently asked questions
        </h2>

        <div class="faq-grid">
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Is Nimbus really free?</h3>
            <p>
              Yes — completely. Bulk migration, nightly scheduling, cache
              purge, cost analytics, page-builder rewriting, WooCommerce
              signed downloads, and multisite network admin are all included
              on every install. There is no license key, no paid tier, and no
              feature held back.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Is there a limit on sites or media files?</h3>
            <p>
              No. Run Nimbus on as many WordPress installations as you want,
              with as much media as you want. There is no activation limit and
              no per-file cap of any kind.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Is Nimbus open source?</h3>
            <p>
              Yes. Nimbus is licensed under GPL-2.0-or-later and its source is
              publicly available. Contributions, bug reports, and feature
              requests are welcome.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Do updates and support ever require payment?</h3>
            <p>
              No. Plugin updates come through WordPress.org like any other
              free plugin, and support is community-based via the
              WordPress.org forum, GitHub issues, and email — no active
              license or subscription required.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Which storage providers does Nimbus support?</h3>
            <p>
              Nimbus ships with nine dedicated provider profiles: Amazon S3,
              Cloudflare R2, Google Cloud Storage, DigitalOcean Spaces,
